---
// B4 — The method (centrepiece). ASSET P2 (workshop photograph) is pending,
// so per its defined absent state the block ships text-only at full width —
// never a stock or AI placeholder. When P2 lands: grid 7/5, photo right,
// 4px radius, hairline, no shadow; photo stacks above text <900px.
// The Harry Jackson pull quote (Q1) is omitted entirely until the real line
// exists — never a paraphrase, never a placeholder (§6/B4).

const rows = [
  { key: "ON SITE", value: "Time where you work, at your events, with your customers" },
  { key: "THE WORD SURVEY", value: "The phrases your customers use that nobody’s competing for" },
  { key: "DIRECTIONS FIRST", value: "Real options before any code — chosen by you" },
  { key: "OPEN LINE", value: "Message me during the build; ideas fold in as they come" },
];
---

<section class="method g-sheet" id="method">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="t-micro eyebrow">HOW THE DIFFERENCE GETS FOUND</p>
    <h2 class="t-h2 method-h2">A brief tells you what a business does. Not why anyone chooses&nbsp;them.</h2>

    <div class="method-body" data-rv>
      <p>
        So before I design anything, I turn up. I’ve stood in David Jackson’s workshop watching
        timber become something that ends up in listed buildings. I’ve been to events with
        WulfTek to hear what their customers actually say about them — not what the website says.
      </p>
      <p>
        That’s where the difference lives, and it never comes out in a questionnaire. It comes
        out on the third visit, in something said offhand.
      </p>
      <p>
        Then we design from that. You see real directions before any code, you tell me what’s
        wrong with them, and you can message me the moment you have a better idea — all the way
        through. It’s just me, so there’s nobody in between.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="method-rows" data-rv>
      {rows.map((row) => (
        <div class="method-row">
          <span class="t-micro row-key">{row.key}</span>
          <span class="row-value">{row.value}</span>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .method { padding-block: 120px; }
  .method-h2 { max-width: 18em; }

  .method-body { margin-top: 32px; }
  .method-body p {
    max-width: 34em;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .method-body p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .method-rows { margin-top: 48px; max-width: 640px; }
  .method-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 150px 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
    align-items: baseline;
    padding-block: 16px;
    border-top: var(--hairline);
  }
  .method-row:last-child { border-bottom: var(--hairline); }
  .row-key { color: var(--color-graphite); }
  .row-value { color: var(--color-ink); }

  @media (max-width: 639.98px) {
    .method { padding-block: 96px; }
    .method-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 4px; }
  }
</style>
